* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sln text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Anything a Linux container executes must keep LF endings. A CRLF shebang line makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter named "/bin/sh\r", which fails with a message that names neither.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
dockerfile text eol=lf
